Feature: the cursor and popup widgets, to an embedder that draws off-screen.

zebkit's off-screen views (<zebkit/offscreen.h>) have no window: the
application draws their frames and sends them input. Two things a page
asks of its window have no public way out of content: the cursor it wants
over itself, and a popup widget it shows (a <select>'s list, a date or
colour picker), whose frames the embedder captures and draws over the page.
content::SetEmbedderWidgetHooks() gives the embedder both, from
RenderWidgetHostImpl::SetCursor() and WebContentsImpl::ShowCreatedWidget().
A new header, so that only the two files that call the hooks build again.

